  "findings": [
    "The previously reported via3 comparison addressed the wrong etch stage. Native APB failures are via4 at the metal4 plane.",
    "Each of the three APB nets has 0.213 um2 gate and one 0.64 um2 via4 cut. The ratio 3.00469483568075 is below six before diode credit.",
    "Native Magic uses contact dimensions in CIF units with tile dimensions in internal units, causing the known via3/via4 arrays to be undercounted.",
    "Native Magic counts overlapping contact fragments as at least one cut each, producing a false failure for one legal stacked via4 cut. All four native misclassifications remain preserved.",
    "All thirteen supplemental stages pass on the unchanged reference GDS files and classify all ten exact-cut controls correctly.",
    "178 independent rational controls cover every stage boundary, diode area and fixed bonus, substrate shorts, future and disconnected protection, two connected gates, unrelated metal and one-time bonus on multiple diodes.",
    "Windows/Linux raw-marker audits agree. 24 native-evidence rejection and rule-inventory unit tests pass on both systems."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The rule-specific rectangular coupons isolate antenna arithmetic and connectivity and are not complete geometry-legal chips.",
    "The logging-only APB trace has 4000 parsed records out of 4003 prefixes; three interleaved records are not claimed reconstructed. The raw log is retained.",
    "Native execution uses the installed Linux KLayout 0.30.5 binary. Windows independently audits the exact reports; fresh consumer delivery is not claimed.",
    "The earlier all-stage v1 record incorrectly carried via4-only metadata; its execution is preserved as diagnostic but not used for the all-stage claim.",
    "Complete rule applicability, density/fill, strict final-GDS LVS, production integration and delivery acceptance remain open."
  ],
